CommitDate: Wed Sep 23 07:17:34 2026 -0500

    fix: deny glibc-routed clock_adjtime(305) variant and repair BPF fall-through skip in seccomp filter. Addresses TJ-DF-020.
    - Add NR 305 (clock_adjtime) to the x86_64 deny table: glibc routes adjtimex()/clock_adjtime() through it, so a filter pinning only adjtimex(159) let libc wrappers bypass the filter. settimeofday->clock_settime(227), init_module->finit_module(313), kexec_load->kexec_file_load(320) variants were already covered; aarch64 mirroring deferred with a TODO until that table is audited on an aarch64 host.
    
    - Fix pre-existing BPF fall-through bug in _build_filter: BPF jf offsets are relative to the next instruction, but non-last JEQ chain entries used jf=1, skipping every second JEQ. Nine deny NRs (incl. 305 at odd chain position) were never consulted; the live patch-b probe (jf 1->0) plus BPF simulation prove all 18 deny NRs now hit the deny block. Regression tests: libc-wrapper EPERM battery (adjtimex, clock_adjtime via ctypes wrappers), raw deny-NR battery, deny-set assertions, getpid default-allow sanity.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
